-- WordPress Connector — the remaining WP Activity Log tables (additive delta, generated by `mj sync push`)
--
-- Adds four objects on top of the 1.1.0 catalog: ActivityLogSession, ActivityLogNotification,
-- ActivityLogGeneratedReport and ActivityLogPeriodicReport. Additive ONLY: 4 IntegrationObject rows
-- and their 58 IntegrationObjectField rows, touching nothing an earlier migration seeded, so a tenant
-- already on 1.1.0 upgrades without a catalog reset.
--
-- All four are served by the companion plugin in Platform/WordPress/wp-plugin/mj-wsal-bridge over the
-- mj-wsal/v1 namespace. Unlike the two objects added in 1.1.0, these four read tables created by WP
-- Activity Log PREMIUM extensions: on a site without them the bridge answers 503 naming the missing
-- table, rather than an empty-but-successful page that would read as "there is no activity".
--
-- Do not hand-edit; the statements below are the generator's own output, sliced to the new records.

